35-000-base-salary-10-hours-ot-week\",\"text\":\"Example 2: $35,000 Base Salary, 10 Hours OT/Week\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"example-3-75-000-base-salary-8-hours-ot-week\",\"text\":\"Example 3: $75,000 Base Salary, 8 Hours OT/Week\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"the-sunset-date-what-happens-after-2028\",\"text\":\"The Sunset Date: What Happens After 2028?\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"what-should-you-do-about-the-sunset\",\"text\":\"What Should You Do About the Sunset?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"state-by-state-impact-where-you-live-matters\",\"text\":\"State-by-State Impact: Where You Live Matters\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"states-with-no-income-tax-maximum-benefit\",\"text\":\"States With No Income Tax (Maximum Benefit)\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"states-with-income-tax-reduced-benefit\",\"text\":\"States With Income Tax (Reduced Benefit)\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"states-that-may-pass-matching-exemptions\",\"text\":\"States That May Pass Matching Exemptions\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"before-vs-after-a-side-by-side-comparison\",\"text\":\"Before vs. After: A Side-by-Side Comparison\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"in-texas-no-state-income-tax\",\"text\":\"In Texas (No State Income Tax)\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"in-california-high-state-income-tax\",\"text\":\"In California (High State Income Tax)\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"how-to-make-sure-you-re-getting-the-exemption\",\"text\":\"How to Make Sure You're Getting the Exemption\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"common-misconceptions\",\"text\":\"Common Misconceptions\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"impact-on-tax-brackets-and-withholding\",\"text\":\"Impact on Tax Brackets and Withholding\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"the-bigger-picture-how-this-fits-into-your-overall-tax-strategy\",\"text\":\"The Bigger Picture: How This Fits Into Your Overall Tax Strategy\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"retirement-contributions\",\"text\":\"Retirement Contributions\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"earned-income-tax-credit-eitc\",\"text\":\"Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC)\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"student-loan-payments\",\"text\":\"Student Loan Payments\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"health-insurance-subsidies\",\"text\":\"Health Insurance Subsidies\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"frequently-asked-questions\",\"text\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"does-the-no-tax-on-overtime-law-apply-to-me-if-i-m-self-employed\",\"text\":\"Does the No Tax on Overtime law apply to me if I'm self-employed?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"is-overtime-really-exempt-from-all-federal-taxes\",\"text\":\"Is overtime really exempt from ALL federal taxes?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"what-if-my-employer-pays-overtime-at-2x-instead-of-1-5x\",\"text\":\"What if my employer pays overtime at 2x instead of 1.5x?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"does-this-apply-to-state-income-tax-too\",\"text\":\"Does this apply to state income tax too?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"what-happens-when-the-law-expires-in-2028\",\"text\":\"What happens when the law expires in 2028?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"how-do-i-know-if-i-m-classified-as-exempt-or-non-exempt\",\"text\":\"How do I know if I'm classified as exempt or non-exempt?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"will-this-exemption-affect-my-tax-refund\",\"text\":\"Will this exemption affect my tax refund?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"can-i-claim-this-exemption-on-my-tax-return-if-my-employer-didn-t-apply-it\",\"text\":\"Can I claim this exemption on my tax return if my employer didn't apply it?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"does-overtime-pay-count-toward-the-social-security-wage-base\",\"text\":\"Does overtime pay count toward the Social Security wage base?\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"final-thoughts\",\"text\":\"Final Thoughts\",\"level\":2}]}]}]}],\"$L29\"]}],\"$L2a\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Author: Rachel Mitchell\",\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/5 to-card/80 p-5 sm:p-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/author-rachel-mitchell.webp\",\"alt\":\"Rachel Mitchell, CPA\",\"width\":48,\"height\":48,\"className\":\"h-12 w-12 shrink-0 rounded-full object-cover ring-1 ring-emerald-500/30\",\"loading\":\"lazy\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-w-0 flex-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L11\",null,{\"href\":\"/about#rachel-mitchell\",\"className\":\"text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-emerald-400 transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Rachel Mitchell\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-emerald-500/15 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-400 ring-1 ring-emerald-500/25\",\"children\":\"CPA\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Lead Tax Analyst & Editorial Director\",\", TheTaxCalc\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2\",\"children\":\"Rachel Mitchell is a Certified Public Accountant (CPA) licensed in Illinois with over 12 years of experience in individual and small-business taxation. She specializes in federal and state income tax compliance, FICA optimization, payroll tax strategy, and multi-state tax planning. Rachel holds an MS in Taxation from Golden Gate University and a BS in Accounting from the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign. She is an active member of the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants (AICPA) and the Illinois CPA Society. Before joining TheTaxCalc, Rachel spent 8 years at a Big Four accounting firm advising high-net-worth clients on tax-efficient wealth strategies.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-3 w-3 text-emerald-500/60\",\"fill\":\"none\